From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:40:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 096/162] hjviewer: review fixes, gate1 lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A0 note on phones: a phone's sessions share one FFI session ID, so the
once-a-session guard of the PC password box's note is re-armed at each
connect() there; A0 and later sessions to a held PC note again.

LK1 title: the PC's ID moves from the one-line title, which cut it at
360 dp and on 390 pt iPhones, into the wrapping text ("PC {ID}에
연결할까요?", the ID's groups kept on one line); the title is now
"링크로 연결" / "Connect from a link".

X-17 binding: when a phone's link skipped LK1 for A0 and A0 is no longer
due at connect() (the mode changed meanwhile), connect() asks LK1 there
and opens only on [연결]; _askTarget returns the session's ID with the
decision, so no second bridge call is needed.

Terminal admin mark: A0 and LK1 (at connect() and for a desktop link)
take the IS_TERMINAL_ADMIN mark down while they ask and set it again only
when the session opens, as hjvOfferWake does, so [취소] does not hand it
to the next terminal.

Tests: the A0 Enter rule, the link step, the 30 s link note and the
connect-time choice are pure functions in hjviewer_access_texts.dart,
which the dialogs call, tested in hjviewer_access_test.dart.

hjv-gate links: a link that opens nothing no longer brings the main
window up; the tray's login waits for the overlay as LK1 does.

dart format on the three files.

